{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/961284-playing-a-spirit","id":961284,"title":"Playing a Spirit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-31T16:44:44-07:00","id":961284,"title":"Playing a Spirit?","content":"I've got a player interested in playing a spirit. I have the Chronicles of Darkness, WtF 2.0 and the Pack. As far as I can see I've got the mechanics to play one, and a way to give it XP, but no starting point to keep it similarly balanced to starting werewolves (the pack does have some xp but it's still early in the adventure).<br /> If I understand spirits correctly, to be self aware and unique enough to be a PC, he'd have to start ar rank 2? Any help or hints (or page numbers if I'm a ditz and missed them) would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6533-gingerkid88","name":"Gingerkid88","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:01:33-07:00","id":961735,"title":"","content":"Page 64 of <b>The Pack </b>has Experience costs for everything necessary to the operation of a spirit. Rank 3 is when the Spirits start being treated like an actual person by other Spirits. Rank 2 is more of a child, and Rank 1 is something equivalent to an infant or an animal. Just bear in mind that, while a Spirit is generally going to have a <i>significantly </i>larger dice pool than some of the other characters, they also don't have Skills and they're reliant upon a set of pretty restrictive Conditions. Also, all of their abilities cost a <i>lot </i>of Essence and a Spirit doesn't have an easy way to regain Willpower except for gorging itself on Essence.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, if you have a larger group, you could have this player who wants to play a Spirit play the Totem of the Pack? That would get around most of the issues of playing a low-power Spirit, and also most of the issues of Manifestation Conditions.<br /> <br /> You'd also need to tag some sort of Beat mechanic to the Manifestation Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 09-01-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:10:53-07:00","id":961818,"title":"","content":"The starting xp loadout for a supernatural character is 107 Experiences. For a mortal, it's 99 Experiences.<br /> <br /> That might be a bit strong for playing a spirit, since that can lead to some pretty potent starting Attributes. One may want to cut the amount of Experiences from Attributes by 2/3, since every point in an ephemeral Attribute is 3x as effective.<br /> <br /> This would give a starting Experiences Pool of 70 for the purchase of initial Attributes, Influences, and Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}